water,liquid,tabulated,,,,,,,water.mienk,998,0.3,1.1,"n from Daimon-Masumura 4-term Sellmeier folds to only 3 terms with 2e-3 error over 400-700nm (>1e-4 tolerance), so tabulated route used instead per spec; k(500nm)~1e-9, shows weak absorption shoulder near 975nm","Daimon & Masumura 2007, Appl. Opt. 46, 3811 (n, 20C HPLC water) + Hale & Querry 1973, Appl. Opt. 12, 555 (k, 25C); combined in nk_data/water.csv"
glass,glass,constant,1.52,0.0,,,,,,2500,0.35,2.0,"generic soda-lime glass placeholder used by example GlassSphere geometry; not a specific catalog glass","Generic soda-lime glass n~1.52 (common textbook/handbook value)"
polystyrene,polymer,sellmeier,1.4435,0.0,0.0,0.020216,1.0,1.0,,1050,0.4368,1.052,"one-term Sellmeier (formula-2 style, C in um^2 directly, not squared); verified n(589nm)=1.59155 vs target 1.5916","Sultanova, Kasarova & Nikolov 2009, Acta Phys. Pol. A 116, 585; coefficients per refractiveindex.info fit"
latex,polymer,sellmeier,1.4435,0.0,0.0,0.020216,1.0,1.0,,1050,0.4368,1.052,"alias of polystyrene optical constants -- real latex microsphere n depends on formulation/hydration; used because example/user scripts refer to material 'latex'","Same as polystyrene: Sultanova, Kasarova & Nikolov 2009 (approximation; latex modeled as polystyrene optically)"
